! C22-6578 PROBLEM 3.2, "INTEGER PART OF FLOATING-POINT WORD", printed
! p.26 (PDF 27), read in the ink.
!
!   "The floating-point number N in location DOG is defined as in the
!   previous problem.  Put the lowest 18-bits of the VFL integer
!   corresponding to I into the first 18-bits of the count field of $1."
!
!   Method 1.   DL(U), DOG
!               D+(U), X48
!               ST(BU, 18), 17.28, 68   '$1.28 is also acceptable
!               BEW, $
!       X48     DD(N), 0.0X48
!
! The five printed statements are the deck's last five before its data,
! as printed.  Blocks A and B are the same three instructions on other
! data with DOG renamed; block B uses the page's other spelling, $1.28.
! Each block is preceded by the deck's own LX, $1, PAT, which fills $1
! with a pattern so that a store that reached outside the count field
! would show, and blocks A and B are followed by the deck's own SX to
! keep what $1 held.
!
! ASSEMBLED WITH ASM=strap2: see problem_3_1.strap.
!
! THE EXPECTED VALUES ARE HAND-DERIVED:
!   After D+(U), X48 the integer part of N is in accumulator bits 12-59
!   with its units bit at bit 59 (problem_3_1.strap's header, Reference
!   Manual printed p.86-87 and p.95).  An offset of 68 names the field
!   whose right end is 68 bits from the accumulator's right end, bit
!   127: bit 59.  So the 18 bits stored are accumulator bits 42-59, the
!   lowest 18 bits of the integer, and BU stores no sign.
!   The count field of an index word is bits 28-45, 18 bits; 17.28 is
!   word 17 ($1) bit 28.  Nothing else in $1 may change.
!
!   PAT is A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5.  Its bits 28-45 are replaced:
!     block  N            integer  lowest 18 bits   $1 afterwards
!     A      -7.25        7        7                A5A5A5A0001DA5A5
!     B      1048581.5    2^20+5   5                A5A5A5A00015A5A5
!     last   2.5          2        2                A5A5A5A00009A5A5
!   (the count sits at bits 28-45, so the hexadecimal digit that holds
!   its two lowest bits also holds the pattern's bits 46-47, 01:
!   7 -> 1D, 5 -> 15, 2 -> 09; A5A5A5A before it and A5A5 after it are
!   the pattern's own.)
!
!   Block B is the reason for "lowest 18-bits": the integer has 21.
!
! INJECTION, OBSERVED 2026-11-15 (data side, on a copy of the deck, the
! deck itself untouched): DOGA changed from -29/4 to -37/4 (-9.25).  FAIL A_count only
! (got a5a5a5a00025a5a5); the other two checks and the PC passed.

START   LX, $1, PAT
        DL(U), DOGA
        D+(U), X48
        ST(BU, 18), 17.28, 68
        SX, $1, RESA
        LX, $1, PAT
        DL(U), DOGB
        D+(U), X48
        ST(BU, 18), $1.28, 68
        SX, $1, RESB
        LX, $1, PAT
! --- the page, as printed -------------------------------------------
        DL(U), DOG
        D+(U), X48
        ST(BU, 18), 17.28, 68
        BEW, $
X48     DD(N), 0.0X48
! --- the deck's data ------------------------------------------------
DOG     DD(N), 5/2
DOGA    DD(N), -29/4
DOGB    DD(N), 2097163/2
PAT     DD(BU, 64), 11936128518282651045
RESA    DR(BU, 64), (1)
RESB    DR(BU, 64), (1)
        END, START
